From f17a6a9fe34546796abcc3e74ca836170b7122c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Illya Antonyuk <illantalex84@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:52:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 52/73] misc: p1i-modem: the Sony Ericsson P1i's modem link
 (UART3)

The P1i's DB2001 modem talks CAIF serial on UART3, which Symbian sets
up (115200 8N1, FIFOs, clock divider) and keeps a break on while idle.
Under the 8250 driver the modem stopped taking frames, and two of four
fresh boots froze when the port was first opened: 8250 rewrites line
control and FIFOs and lifts the break on every open and close.

This driver uses the UART as the boot firmware left it: no register
writes at probe; open enables the receive interrupts, read/poll take
the received bytes from a buffer, write returns once the last stop bit
is out, TIOCSBRK/TIOCCBRK set and clear the break, and release leaves
the break on. Receive overruns are counted in sysfs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/misc/Kconfig     |   9 ++
 drivers/misc/Makefile    |   1 +
 drivers/misc/p1i-modem.c | 319 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 329 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/p1i-modem.c

